//! WHERE A VALUE IS ASKED FOR WHAT ITS TYPE DOESN'T HAVE: a field read a record doesn't declare
//! and no property or method of its type answers, a method call no method, static or field of a
//! declared type answers, and `[…]` on a value that's no list. Read over a written item's bodies and
//! the statements its file runs, as the program layer types them, the type's members asked as typing
//! asks them; a generated item's nodes are judged as its own and said at the annotation that made
//! it, while a node a template copies into a written item, or a body an annotation wraps, is typed
//! apart from the file's own nodes, so it has none here.
